// Rstest Snapshot v1

exports[`the background's catalogue > animation_canceled: the message 1`] = `
"The animation fade of the <view> was canceled before it finished.

Nothing to fix when the animation was canceled on purpose. Catch the rejection of finished where a canceled animation matters.
https://sohedra.com/e/animation_canceled"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > attribute_not_copyable: the message 1`] = `
"The value of accessibility-actions on <view> cannot be sent to the main thread (Do not know how to serialize a BigInt), so the element does not get it.

Give the attribute plain data: strings, numbers, booleans, null, arrays and plain objects, without cycles or BigInt values.
https://sohedra.com/e/attribute_not_copyable"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > background_function_missing: the message 1`] = `
"A main-thread function called a background function through runOnBackground, and the background no longer has it: the page let go of the main-thread function that named it.

Keep main-thread functions that call the background in an attribute, a ref or a call that is still on the page. If the page was made again after its first frame could not be hydrated, functions kept from before cannot call the background.
https://sohedra.com/e/background_function_missing"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > element_not_on_page: the message 1`] = `
"The <view> is not on the page, so its boundingClientRect cannot run: Lynx has no element for it.

Call boundingClientRect once the element is on the page: in an attachment, an effect or an event handler, not while the component is being built or after the element was removed.
https://sohedra.com/e/element_not_on_page"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > element_not_shown: the message 1`] = `
"The <view> is in a list row Lynx is not showing, so its boundingClientRect cannot run: Lynx makes a row's elements only while it shows the row.

Call boundingClientRect while Lynx shows the row, for example from the row's layoutchange event.
https://sohedra.com/e/element_not_shown"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > hydration_mismatch: the message 1`] = `
"The first frame did not match the page the background rendered: the <view>'s class is "card" on the background and "card wide" in the first frame. The page was made again.
src/Card.svelte:4:1

Render the same markup on both threads from the page's data. Keep what only the background knows (a value an effect sets, the time, a random number) in an effect, or in {#if background} from @sohedra/lynx/env.
https://sohedra.com/e/hydration_mismatch"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > initial_item_count_not_a_count: the message 1`] = `
"A <list>'s initial-item-count is "three", which is not a number of rows, so its first frame draws as many rows as it would without it.
src/Feed.svelte:7:0

Give initial-item-count a whole number of rows, 0 or more: initial-item-count={5} or initial-item-count="5".
https://sohedra.com/e/initial_item_count_not_a_count"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > initial_scroll_index_past_first_screen: the message 1`] = `
"A <list> starts at initial-scroll-index 150, more than 100 rows down, so its first frame draws only its first rows, and the deferred rows it starts at are empty until the background renders them.
src/Feed.svelte:7:0

Start the list at most 100 rows down, or take defer off the rows it starts at.
https://sohedra.com/e/initial_scroll_index_past_first_screen"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > input_value_not_written: the message 1`] = `
"The value of the <input> element could not be written: Lynx answered setValue with the code 4.

Check that the element is still on the page when its value changes, and that it is an <input> or a <textarea>.
https://sohedra.com/e/input_value_not_written"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > list_item_defer_needs_async_list: the message 1`] = `
"A <list-item defer> is in a <list> without custom-list-name="list-container", so its row renders now instead of waiting until Lynx asks for it.
src/Feed.svelte:9:3

Give the list custom-list-name="list-container", the list that waits for a row Lynx asked for. Or remove defer.
https://sohedra.com/e/list_item_defer_needs_async_list"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > list_item_key_object: the message 1`] = `
"A <list-item> has an object as its item-key, and Lynx reads an item-key as text.
src/Feed.svelte:12:2

Key the item with a string or a number that names it, such as its id: {#each items as item (item.id)}, or item-key={item.id}.
https://sohedra.com/e/list_item_key_object"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > main_thread_event_spelling_removed: the message 1`] = `
"The <view>'s main-thread:bindtap uses Lynx's own spelling of an event, which a component no longer writes.
src/Sheet.svelte:14:2

Write main-thread:ontap instead.
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_event_spelling_removed"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > main_thread_ref_read_on_background: the message 1`] = `
"The current value of a main-thread ref was read on the background, where it is only the ref's initial value: the ref's value lives on the main thread.

Read it inside a main-thread function. To get it on the background, return it from one: await runOnMainThread(read)().
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_ref_read_on_background"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > main_thread_ref_set_on_background: the message 1`] = `
"The current value of a main-thread ref was set on the background: the ref's value lives on the main thread, and only main-thread functions set it.

Set it inside a main-thread function, and call that from the background with runOnMainThread(set)(value).
https://sohedra.com/e/main_thread_ref_set_on_background"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > not_a_main_thread_function: the message 1`] = `
"The value given to runOnMainThread, measure, is not a main-thread function, so nothing runs on the main thread.

Start the function's body with the 'main thread' directive, and pass the function itself: runOnMainThread(fn)(...args).
https://sohedra.com/e/not_a_main_thread_function"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > page_is_gone: the message 1`] = `
"A call of scrollTo has no answer: the page it was made on has been closed or reloaded.

Nothing to fix when the page closed on purpose. Otherwise, make the call again on the page that is open now.
https://sohedra.com/e/page_is_gone"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > plain_function_under_main_thread: the message 1`] = `
"The <view>'s main-thread:ontap is a plain function, so the main thread binds nothing: a main-thread attribute takes a main-thread function.
src/Sheet.svelte:14:2

Start the function's body with the 'main thread' directive, or use the attribute without the main-thread: prefix to run it on the background.
https://sohedra.com/e/plain_function_under_main_thread"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > props_id_mismatch: the message 1`] = `
"The <text>'s id is "lynx-s2" in the first frame and "lynx-s3" on the background: $props.id() gave another id on each thread, and the first frame showed its own until the background's replaced it.
src/Field.svelte:8:1

Look before it for a component that only one thread renders, and put it inside {#if background} or {#if mainThread} from @sohedra/lynx/env, or {#if BROWSER} from esm-env, with the flag alone as the test. Or look for a component binding whose child changes the bound value as it starts, which renders the first frame twice: give the value its start in the parent.
https://sohedra.com/e/props_id_mismatch"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > run_on_background_outside_main_thread: the message 1`] = `
"A call of runOnBackground(save) ran on the background: it calls a background function from a main-thread function only.

On the background, call the function itself. Use runOnBackground inside a function whose body starts with 'main thread'.
https://sohedra.com/e/run_on_background_outside_main_thread"
`;

exports[`the background's catalogue > text_outside_text: the message 1`] = `
"The text "Hello" is inside <view>, and Lynx shows text only inside <text>.
src/App.svelte:3:1

Wrap it in <text>: <text>Hello</text>.
https://sohedra.com/e/text_outside_text"
`;
